<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Zürich</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lake Zurich, Zürichsee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Zürich is a lake in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, about 40 kilometres long, stretching south-east from the city of Zürich, which stands where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limmat">Limmat</a> flows out of it. Its shores belong mainly to the canton of Zürich, with parts in Schwyz and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>, and towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rapperswil">Rapperswil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafa">Stäfa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadenswil">Wädenswil</a> lie along them. It was an important route for trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-zurich.jpg" alt="Lake Zürich" width="320" height="112" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pfannenstiel_-_Z%C3%BCrichsee_-_Sihltal_-_Albis_Baldern_IMG_5316.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
